### tb101.static -- the bench facts no `show` command can reveal. Hand-entered, one time.
### Read by bench_probe.py --box tb101 when it generates bench-setup/tb101/bench-state.md / tb101.setup:
###   - a unit's swi_ name follows its SERIAL (names kept from tb470, Test Engineer 2026-10-20);
###   - the outlet is the numeric PDU outlet; "-" = none. tb101 has NO PDU (Test Engineer, 2026-10-20),
###     so no [pdu] section and every outlet is "-": nothing on this bench can be power-cycled.

### serial = name, outlet
[units]
264A23061 = swi_a, -    ### IE520-28GSX, stack member 1, console u0 (2026-10-20)
264A23068 = swi_b, -    ### IE520-28GSX, stack member 2, console u1 (2026-10-20)
264A23052 = swi_d, -    ### IE520-28GSX, stack member 3, console u2 (2026-10-20)
264A23066 = swi_c, -    ### IE520-28GSX, stack member 4, console u3 (2026-10-20)
